# The Unity project lives in "spirit&hearts/", one level below this file.
# Patterns here are deliberately left unanchored so they match inside it.
# A pattern containing a slash (e.g. "ProjectSettings/Foo.asset") anchors to
# this directory and will NOT match the project - see the note at the bottom.

# Unity generated
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
[Mm]emoryCaptures/
.utmp/
*_BurstDebugInformation_DoNotShip/
Generated*/
Exports/

# Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code - all regenerated by Unity
.vs/
.idea/
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb

# Unity Smart Merge leftovers.
# NB: do not write "*.unity.*" here - it also matches every .unity.meta,
# which Unity cannot regenerate without inventing new GUIDs and breaking
# every reference to the scene.
*.orig
*.merges

# Crash reports
sysinfo.txt
crash.log
*.log
mono_crash.*.json

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db

# Unity Asset Store tools
Assets/AssetStoreTools*/

# Play mode save data
Assets/PlayModeSaveData/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, and why:
#
#   Packages/            manifest.json and packages-lock.json pin every
#                        dependency. Ignoring them means a fresh clone
#                        silently resolves a different package set.
#
#   ProjectSettings/     tags, layers, physics, XR and quality settings.
#                        The code resolves objects by the tags defined in
#                        TagManager.asset (MainPlayer, Player, Mountain,
#                        SeedHolster, Light), so losing it breaks the game
#                        at runtime with no compile error.
#
#   *.meta               Unity's identity for every asset. Never ignore these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
